  data: {
    LLM: 'On each turn, draw from stock or discard, optionally lay required meld contracts and lay off, then discard. Each hand has a specific contract requirement (sets/runs combinations). When a player goes out, others score cards left in hand. After ten hands, lowest total score wins.',
    Player: 'On each turn, draw from stock or discard, optionally lay required meld contracts and lay off, then discard. Each hand has a specific contract requirement (sets/runs combinations). When a player goes out, others score cards left in hand. After ten hands, lowest total score wins.',
    objective: 'Finish the ten-hand sequence with the lowest cumulative score.',
    gameplay: 'On each turn, draw from stock or discard, optionally lay required meld contracts and lay off, then discard. Each hand has a specific contract requirement (sets/runs combinations). When a player goes out, others score cards left in hand. After ten hands, lowest total score wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Ten hands with changing contract requirements.',
      'Must meet the hand contract before laying off freely.',
      'Jokers and 2s are commonly wild, subject to table limits.',
      'Players may buy the top discard out of turn under agreed rules.',
